# Caddy reverse proxy for this VPS.
# Runs with `network_mode: host` so Caddy binds directly to host ports 80/443
# and sees real client IPs (required for the tailscale-only remote_ip matcher).
# Backend apps run in sibling compose projects and are reached via their
# localhost port bindings (e.g. reverse_proxy localhost:3001).
#
# To expose a site: point its DNS at this server, uncomment a block
# below with your domain, then run:
#   docker compose exec caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile
#
# TAILSCALE-ONLY SITES (template — set your IPs in tailscale-ips.caddy):
# every site imports `tailscale-only`, which drops any client that is
# NOT on the tailnet. Copy tailscale-ips.caddy.example to
# tailscale-ips.caddy (git-ignored) and put your tailnet IPs there
# (`tailscale ip -4` on each allowed device, plus 127.0.0.1/8 for local
# healthchecks). To add/remove a device, edit the IP list in that ONE file.
# The `not path /.well-known/acme-challenge/*` line lets Let's Encrypt
# HTTP-01 challenges through so certificates can still be issued/renewed.
# For a PUBLIC site instead, just omit `import tailscale-only` from its block.
import tailscale-ips.caddy

{
	# Uncomment for Let's Encrypt expiry notices:
	# email you@example.com
}

